hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"95","Sayyiduna Muawiyah bin Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: I heard my mother, Hind bint Utbah (may Allah be pleased with her), mentioning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and she was saying: On the day of the Battle of Uhud, I mutilated the uncle and companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him). When the Quraysh returned at night, I was with them. I saw a dream for three consecutive nights: I saw that I was in darkness and could not see anything. Suddenly, the darkness was dispelled by light, and I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) calling me. Then, on the second night, I saw that I was on a path, and on my right side was ""Hubal"" and on my left side was ""Isaf,"" calling me, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was in front of me, and he said: Come, come to this path. Then, on the third night, I saw that I was standing at the edge of Hell, and its keepers wanted to throw me into it, and Hubal was saying: Enter into it. I turned and saw that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was standing behind me, holding my clothes, and I moved away from the pit of Hell. I was frightened and said: The truth and falsehood have been made clear to me. In the morning, I went to the idol in my house and broke it, and while breaking it, I was saying: For how long have I been deceived about you! Then I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), accepted Islam, and pledged allegiance to him."
